From 1e4fe8d17e81d84f715618a6ac6ce886db04cbe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thien Trung Vuong <tvuong@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:41:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(libdnf5): expose optional rpm-md package file time in
 C++

Read the retained SOLVABLE_FILETIME directly from the loaded libsolv package metadata. Unlike build time, an absent or nonnumeric file-time key returns nullopt, so consumers can distinguish missing publication time from zero. The public API returns std::optional<unsigned long long>; omit the unsupported optional conversion from the common SWIG interface for Python, Perl and Ruby.

Exercise a present file=123 distinct from build=456 and a missing file attribute in the rpm-md fixture. Update its primary checksum and size and verify the binding remains omitted.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
